From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:22:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/49] Red team fix 7: an index file the rewrite keeps unread
 is first compared with its name

Prune's index rewrite keeps the index files that stay as they are without
decoding them again. Upstream reads every index file again, so it fails on a
file that was damaged or removed after it was loaded; the kept files were not
looked at. Each kept file is now read as it is stored and its SHA-256 compared
with its name (the repository's LoadRaw, with which upstream's reload begins;
content that passes is the content this process decoded before). A file that
cannot be read or has changed fails the rewrite with the error of upstream's
reload, before any index file is removed. What is still saved is the
decryption, decompression and decoding of the kept files. A repository
wrapper without LoadRaw gets upstream's full reload.

Tests: TestRewriteRejectsDamagedKeptIndex (seat 2 finding 3, carried in)
fails before this commit and passes after; TestRewriteKeepsUnread now also
requires one raw read per kept file; TestRewriteFailsOnChangedKeptFile covers
a changed and a missing kept file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
